   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Helping others",
     "texto": [
      "An **asociación** works with **voluntarios**: people who **colaboran** without being paid. They can **repartir** books, **cuidar** **personas mayores**, **hacer compañía** to someone who lives alone, or run a clean-up **campaña**. You can also **donar** clothes, books or money.\n\nHelping fights **soledad**. A **solidaria** person thinks of others.\n\nTo invite someone: **¿Por qué no te apuntas?** **Merece la pena.**\n\nTo say what you wish for others: **quiero que**, **ojalá**, **es importante que** + subjunctive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Wishing something for others",
     "texto": [
      "To say what you want other people to do, use the subjunctive:\n\n- **Quiero que** + subjunctive: **quiero que la gente sepa que no está sola**.\n- **Ojalá** + subjunctive: **ojalá vengas un día**.\n- **Es importante que** + subjunctive: **es importante que todos ayudemos**.\n\nIf the same person wants and does, use the infinitive: **quiero ayudar**, not «quiero que ayude» (for myself).\n\nWith people use the personal **a**: **cuido a mi abuela**, **ayudo a los vecinos**."
     ],
